Title: Ego Hygiene
Credit: Written & Designed by Alan Szmyt
Draft date: 2026-02-15
Source: Edition 1 – Orientation

INT. PRINTED MAGAZINE – REST PAGE – TIMELESS

The next pillar emerges.

REST

Below the arching header:

Practices for Allowing Rest & Recovery

The palette deepens.
The glow softens.
Stars scatter lightly across a darkened sky.

At center,
a figure lies in quiet stillness,
hands folded,
breathing steady.

Above,
a crescent moon rests inside a drifting thought-cloud.

Four practice panels surround the scene.

PAUSE
Stop adding input.
No fixing.
No optimizing.

DIM
Lower light, sound, and stimulation.

DREAM
Allow dreaming and deep imagery.

STAY
Remain at rest when the urge to act appears.

Near the bottom,
a highlighted band reads:

EFFECT:
Allows the nervous system to downshift,
restores baseline regulation,
and reduces cognitive load.

A final declaration anchors the page:

NOTHING IS REQUIRED RIGHT NOW

The page feels like exhale.
Release without collapse.
Stillness without demand.
